\nL320: Pack Size Availability Price\nL321: 25G 【94†Contact us for lead time details - Request Quote】 $36.65 100G 【94†Contact us for lead time details - Request Quote】 $92.54 250G 【94†Contact us for lead time details - Request Quote】 $160.84\nL322: \nL323: Product variants\nL324: \nL325: [Select]\nL326: \nL327: [Input][Input]\nL328: \nL329: [Input][Input][Input][Input][Input]\nL330: \nL331: [Input]\nL332: \nL333: [Button: Add to cart] 【69†Request Bulk Quote】\nL334: \nL335: [Input][Input]\nL336: \nL337: Product Information\nL338: Ammonium magnesium phosphate hexahydrate is a versatile compound known for its unique properties and applications in various fields. This crystalline substance, often referred to as struvite, is primarily utilized in agriculture as a slow-release fertilizer, providing essential nutrients such as nitrogen, phosphorus, and magnesium to plants. Its slow solubility ensures that crops receive a steady supply of nutrients over time, promoting healthy growth and improving yield.\nL339: Additionally, struvite is gaining attention in wastewater treatment processes, where it plays a crucial role in nutrient recovery and the reduction of phosphorus pollution, thus contributing to environmental sustainability.\nL340: Researchers and industry professionals appreciate ammonium magnesium phosphate hexahydrate for its dual functionality in both agricultural and environmental applications. Its ability to enhance soil fertility while simultaneously addressing nutrient runoff makes it a valuable asset in sustainable farming practices.\nL341: Furthermore, the compound's stability and low solubility in water make it an ideal choice for controlled-release formulations, ensuring that nutrients are available to plants when they need them most. This compound stands out among similar fertilizers due to its environmentally friendly profile and effectiveness in promoting plant health.\nL342: [Button: General Information ][Button: Properties ][Button: Applications ]\nL3